The following does not work in `JAX`:
```python
@jit
def mytest(param):
    return np.sqrt(np.sum(param * np.asarray([3.0, 4.0])))
mytest(jnp.ones((1,)))
```

To make this work, one needs:
```python
@jit
def mytest(param):
    return jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(param * np.asarray([3.0, 4.0])))
mytest(jnp.ones((1,)))
```

This caused our `.distance()` to break within a `jit`. This PR fixes it.

This PR started as a way to fix node event input display, but I realized unfortunately that our display classes currently generate:
```python
node_input_ids_by_name = {
    "foo": UUID
}
```

but our templating node events will emit:
```python
node_input_ids_by_name = {
    "inputs.foo": UUID
}
```

The latter is more consistent with "attribute paths" - meaning it will be more extensible to dynamic attributes at any level. So in the meantime, this PR just supports generating input_display when there's no display classes defined, and we'll update vellum side handling to do both

~Gonna block this guy on this one first: https://github.com/vellum-ai/vellum-python-sdks/pull/1130~

Before this PR, we were returning:
```js
display context = {
    nodes: {
        inner_node_id: {
            nodes: {
                outer_node_id
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This unblocked our monitoring in the short term, but now prevents us from showing separate traces invoked by an adornment. By putting it in the correct order, we can now treat adornments as any other subworkflow paradigm.

We'll need to update vellum-side logic before this goes live with version 0.14.15

## Overview
Membuat api `api/filters` yang akan mengembalikan opsi pilihan filter yang bisa digunakan oleh user untuk melakukan filter pada data yang diinginkan. API ini akan mengembalikan data berupa array of object yang berisi key-value pair dari nama penyakit, lokasi, dan sumber berita.
## Fitur yang modifikasi
Seluruh fitur yang ada di dalam API ini adalah fitur baru yang belum ada sebelumnya.
## Tambah/kurang
Tidak ada penambahan atau pengurangan fitur yang dilakukan.
## How to use
API ini dapat diakses dengan menggunakan metode `GET` pada endpoint `/api/filters`. Berikut adalah contoh penggunaan API ini.
### Request
```http
GET /api/filters
```
### Response
```json
{
    "data": {
        "diseases": [
            {
                "value": "HIV",
                "label": "HIV"
            },
            {
                "value": "Flu Singapura",
                "label": "Flu Singapura"
            }
        ],
        "locations": [
            {
                "value": "Bali",
                "label": "Bali"
            },
            {
                "value": "Surabaya",
                "label": "Surabaya"
            },
            {
                "value": "Bogor",
                "label": "Bogor"
            }
        ],
        "news": [
            {
                "value": "Columbia Asia",
                "label": "Columbia Asia"
            },
            {
                "value": "Kompas Id",
                "label": "Kompas Id"
            }
        ]
    }
}
```
Untuk melakukan akses terhadap data yang ada, user perlu memanggil atribut `data` terlebih dahulu, kemudian user dapat mengakses data yang diinginkan dengan memanggil atribut `diseases`, `locations`, atau `news`.
## Future works
- Memperbaiki api endpoints agar seragam dengan api lainnya

## User Authentication

Three user routes were created for authentication and user creation:
```
router.post('/', createUserController);
router.post('/login', loginController);
router.post('/logout', authenticate, logoutController);
```
These routes are for User Creation, Login, and Logout using JWT Auth Token.

